# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationReBootstrap. The reap's frontier D is the minimum over
# every origin (#4615): waiting only for the receiver's writes, the source reaps
# a tombstone a third origin's older write, still on its way to the source,
# then resurrects at the source.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceReapIgnoresThirdOrigin
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the reap waits only for the receiver's writes, so a third origin's write still on its way to the source outlives the delete
PERTURBS: Reap
BOUNDS: Third = TRUE, Reattach = FALSE, MaxHlc = 2

--- FIND
    /\ \A o \in Others : \A i \in (cursor[<<o, s>>] + 1)..Len(wal[o]) : wal[o][i].h > reg[s].h
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: D covers the receiver's writes only.
    /\ \A i \in (cursor[<<r, s>>] + 1)..Len(wal[r]) : wal[r][i].h > reg[s].h
--- END
